    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d471">

                <pb facs="0497" n="413" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp02/pg413"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. No. 763.72112/3475</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul General at Rio de
                        Janeiro</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gottschalk</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-04-12T17:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 12, 1917, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your April 10, 6 p.m. You may inform Lloyd Brazileiro Department knows of no
                    legal obstacle to the transaction to which they refer. Point out, however, that
                    this statement of Department is, of course, made in contemplation of existing
                    conditions only.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
